@startuml ui-security
title Lakehouse UI (BFF) - user authentication and backend calls

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #444444
    ActorBorderColor #2C5D8A
    LifeCycleBorderColor #2C5D8A
    ParticipantBorderColor #2C5D8A
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F0F8
}

actor "User\n(browser)" as U
participant "lakehouse-ui-svc\n(BFF)" as BFF
participant "Keycloak\n(realm: lakehouse,\nclient: lakehouse-ui-client)" as KC
participant "Backend services\n(config / state / scheduler /\ntask-proxy)" as BE

== Login: OAuth2 authorization code flow ==

U -> BFF : GET / (protected page)
BFF --> U : 302 redirect to Keycloak
U -> KC : Authenticate (login form)
KC --> U : Redirect to /login/oauth2/code/keycloak\n(authorization code)
U -> BFF : GET callback with code
BFF -> KC : Exchange code for tokens\n(client secret, server-to-server)
KC --> BFF : ID / access / refresh tokens
note over BFF : OAuth2AuthenticationToken created;\nroles from Keycloak claims
BFF --> U : 200 OK\nSet-Cookie: JSESSIONID (HttpOnly),\nXSRF-TOKEN cookie (readable by JS)

== Authenticated usage ==

U -> BFF : API call with session cookie\n+ X-XSRF-TOKEN header
note over BFF : CSRF validated (CookieCsrfTokenRepository);\nwhitelist without auth:\n/actuator/**, /healthz, /readyz, /favicon.ico

BFF -> KC : POST /token\ngrant_type=client_credentials\nclient_id=lakehouse-internal-client
KC --> BFF : access_token (service account)

note over BFF #FFF3D6
    Session holds OAuth2AuthenticationToken
    (not JwtAuthenticationToken) ->
    user JWT is NOT relayed;
    backend calls always use the
    service-account token
end note

BFF -> BE : REST request\nAuthorization: Bearer <service-account JWT>
BE -> BE : JWT validation + role conversion
BE -> BE : AuditLoggingFilter -> AUDIT_LOG (JSON)\nusername = "system" (service account)
BE --> BFF : JSON response
BFF --> U : JSON response

@enduml
